	["旅店老板莎希因"] = { "Your body looks worn and your spirit weary. Rest yourself beneath our roof and allow Elune to guide your dreams." },
	["旅店老板菲兹格瑞博"] = { "Ah a visitor! Must be an adventurer, we don't get many tourists down this way. Grab a chair and a drink, make yourself comfortable. Say, you look like you have some meat on your bones. You thinkin about competing in the cage matches?" },
	["旅店老板詹妮"] = { "Welcome to my Inn, weary traveler. What can I do for you?" },
	["旅店老板诺曼"] = { "Rest your weary bones for a spell." },
	["旅店老板贝尔姆"] = { "Fill yer tankard and pull up a chair. We've stories to tell and kegs to empty.", "What can you do at an inn? Well when you stay at an inn, you rest very comfortably. Because of this, you will become \"well rested\" much more quickly than you would in the wilderness. When you are well rested, you learn more from experience. You may also speak with any innkeeper to get a hearthstone, and can later use the hearthstone in order to quickly return to that inn." },
	["旅店老板贝茨"] = { "Rest your weary bones for a spell.", "What can you do at an inn? Well when you stay at an inn, you rest very comfortably. Because of this, you will become \"well rested\" much more quickly than you would in the wilderness. When you are well rested, you learn more from experience. You may also speak with any innkeeper to get a hearthstone, and can later use the hearthstone in order to quickly return to that inn." },
	["旅店老板贝莉比"] = { "Welcome. Will you take your rest here, or perhaps a meal?" },
	["旅店老板赫布瑞克"] = { "Fill yer tankard and pull up a chair. We've stories to tell and kegs to empty." },
	["旅店老板达尔格·血爪"] = { "If we are to make these new lands ours then we must have places to rest our battle weary bodies. Lay your axe by the fire and share the stories of your mighty battles.", "What can you do at an inn? Well when you stay at an inn, you rest very comfortably. Because of this, you will become \"well rested\" much more quickly than you would in the wilderness. When you are well rested, you learn more from experience. You may also speak with any innkeeper to get a hearthstone, and can later use the hearthstone in order to quickly return to that inn." },
	["旅店老板雷米·度苏"] = { "I hope these Shattrath folks stop fighting soon. They're beginning to get on my nerves. How can I help you?", "These people arrived from Shattrath a few nights ago and they haven't stopped arguing since then. I'm glad to see that hasn't turned you away, I was beginning to think they were scaring off potential customers." },
	["无所不知的威尔特"] = { "A Hero's Welcome is located right beside the Silver Enclave in southwestern Dalaran. The place boasts a beer garden and one of the city's finest cooking trainer in its kitchen.", "Adventurers turn in their Emblems of Heroism or Valor in the Alliance and Horde quarters, in the Silver Enclave or Sunreaver's Sanctuary.", "Adventurers turn in their Emblems of Heroism or Valor in the Silver Enclave or Sunreaver's Sanctuary.", "Aimee's cart can usually be found in northern Dalaran, near the Bank of Dalaran.", "Applebough's fruit cart is usually in southwest Dalaran, near the Silver Enclave.", "Cooking trainers are located in the kitchens of the Alliance and Horde inns in their respective quarters.", "Dalaran has no auction house of its own. You must take a portal back to one of your capitals. They can be found in Dalaran's Alliance and Horde quarters: the Silver Enclave and the Sunreaver's Sancturary.", "Dalaran's arena and those who service it are found beneath the city, in the sewers. There are at least three ways in: Entrances in the east and west, and a well in the north.", "Dalaran's guild master is found in the visitor center, just south of the city's center.", "Dalaran's only class trainers are mages. You must take a portal back to one of your capitals for others. They can be found in Dalaran's Alliance and Horde quarters: the Silver Enclave and the Sunreaver's Sancturary.", "Dalaran's stable master is located inside the Magical Menagerie in northeast Dalaran.", "Do you see the massive spired tower in eastern Dalaran? That is the majestic Violet Citadel.", "Engineers often train at Like Clockwork in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "Glorious Goods in southern Dalaran should have all the general goods you need.", "If you are seeking a locksmith, might I suggest the sewers? That's where you'll find more... disreputable types.", "Jepetto Joybuzz' Wonderworks in western Dalaran carries such items.", "Jepetto Joybuzz's Wonderworks in western Dalaran carries such items.", "Krasus' Landing is in easternmost Dalaran. The city's flight master is there, as well as the cold weather flying trainer.", "Langrom's Leather & Links in southern Dalaran should have what you seek.", "Look for the potion-shaped door to the Agronomical Apothecary in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran. It's quite impossible to miss!", "Miners trainers and supplies are found in the All that Glitters Prospecting Co. in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "One can learn to fish near the enchanted fountain in the Eventide, a square in southern Dalaran.", "Please respect the laws of Dalaran while you are here, stranger. Were you lost? Is there something I might help you find?", "Portals to the various capitals and battlegrounds can be found in Dalaran's Alliance and Horde quarters: the Silver Enclave and the Sunreaver's Sancturary.", "Red at Glorious Goods in southeast Dalaran can provide most general trade supplies. If you need something more specialized, try the Magus Commerce Exchange. Each trade shop there has its own supply vendor.", "Runeweaver Square is a park at the very heart of Dalaran.", "Seek out The Scribe's Sacellum in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "Skinners and leatherworkers of all sorts may be Legendary Leathers in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "Tanks for Everything in northern Dalaran is the city's most popular plate armor and shield merchant.", "That would be Cartier & Co. Fine Jewelry in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "The Arsenal Absolute in southeast Dalaran carries all manner of melee weapons.", "The Bank of Dalaran is in the northern part of the city.", "The Dalaran Merchants' Bank is in the southern part of the city, off the Eventide.", "The Eventide is a square in southern Dalaran. The enchanted fountain there is popular for fishing.", "The Hunter's Reach in eastern Dalaran sells guns, bows, ammunition and the like.", "The Magical Menagerie is located in northeast Dalaran. Pet supplies, exotic mounts, and stables are all available there.", "The Magus Commerce Exchange is in northwest Dalaran, and holds most of the city's profession trainers.", "The Militant Mystic in southern Dalaran should have what you desire.", "The Threads of Fate in western Dalaran is the city's most popular supplier of clothing and cloth armor.", "The Violet Hold, prison for the enemies of the Kirin Tor, is in southeast Dalaran.", "The ancient tomes are always found near inscription trainers.", "The city's best tailors are in Talismanic Textiles in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "The city's best-known barber shop is located in northern Dalaran.", "The city's cemetery is just north of the Violet Citadel in western Dalaran.", "The city's mage and portal trainers may be found in a large building in eastern Dalaran, between Runeweaver Square at the heart of the city and Krasus' Landing.", "The city's premier urgent care center, First to your Aid, is located in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran.", "The eastern sewers entrance is just outside the entrance to Krasus' Landing.", "The high elf Hira Snowdawn teaches Cold Weather Flying. She can be found upon her dragonhawk at Krasus' Landing in eastern Dalaran.", "The memorial park to Antonidas is located in northern Dalaran.", "The most popular inn in Dalaran is the Legerdemain Lounge, just north of the city's center. The Alliance and Horde Quarters each have their own inns as well, and I am told there is one more beneath the city, in the sewers.", "The various merchants of Curiosities & Moore in southern Dalaran sell trinkets, relics, heirlooms, and off-hand items of all sorts.", "The visiting Horde keep primarily to the Sunreaver's Sanctuary in northeastern Dalaran. There is an inn there, as well as portals to the various Horde cities and battlegrounds.", "The western sewers entrance is beneath the stairway to the Violet Citadel.", "There are at least three ways beneath Dalaran: Sewer entrances in the east and west, and a well in the north.", "There are many mailboxes in Dalaran: On many corners, outside nearly every inn and bank, even upon Krasus' Landing.", "There are many places of interest in Dalaran. Which do you seek?", "There are three banks in the city: The Bank of Dalaran in the north, the Dalaran Merchants' Bank in the south, and one more beneath the city, in the sewers.", "There is a greenhouse attached to the Agronomical Apothecary in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran. You'll find the city's best herbalists there.", "There is a large smithy and forge in the Magus Commerce Exchange, northwest Dalaran. Look for the massive enchanted anvil and stained glass windows in he shapes of axes and shields.", "There is well in northern Dalaran that some of the city's more... adventurous... visitors use to enter the sewers.", "Visiting members of the Alliance keep primarily to the Silver Enclave in southwestern Dalaran. There is an inn there, as well as portals to the various Alliance cities and battlegrounds.", "Welcome to Dalaran, traveler. Is there something I might help you find?", "What sort of armor?", "What sort of trainer were you trying to find?", "What sort of weapons?", "Which profession trainer were you looking for?", "Which vendor where you seeking?", "You can normally find Miss Primrose's flower stand in southeast Dalaran.", "You'll find reagants and more at the Sisters Sorcerous in western Dalaran. Just mind the Mooreheads' black cat...", "You'll find the city's Flight Master at Krasus' Landing in eastern Dalaran.", "You'll find what you are looking for at One More Glass in northern Dalaran.", "You'll want to visit Simply Enchanting, just outside the Magus Commerce Exchange in northwest Dalaran.", "You're looking for The Filthy Animal in the Horde quarter of Sunreaver's Sanctuary, northeastern Dalaran. I am told it is a rather rough place, but with an excellent cooking trainer in its kitchen." },
	["无眠者赞扎"] = { "A friend of the Zandalrian! You have ventured deep into the lair of the Blood God, $c. You will do well to listen to what I have to say. Many thousands of years ago, while the indigenous trolls of the Zul'Aman empire were battling the invading high elf heathens, great magic was stolen from Zanza. This magic was used by the high elves to enchant their weapons and armor to assist in conquering the trolls of the region.", "Have you? Then you know how weak and pathetic the high elf version of troll magic was? The high elves could not understand why a people with their magical affinity could not contend with the powers of troll voodoo. This was an inconceivable notion for the pale skins to understand. They were resigned to using the bastardized version of troll enchantments. I believe they called them 'Arcanum.'", "I am Zanza, a Loa of Zandalar. I have come in this ethereal form from Zandalar to help my people. Hakkar has no dominion over my soul. I help those that have helped the Zandalarian people.", "The first is a primal token that must be taken from the most powerful of the Hakkari. The second is a punctured voodoo doll. These can be found in the piles of refuse that litter this foul place. Look inside the jinxed Hoodoo piles. The last is the high elven facsimile of troll magic known as the Arcanum. I do not know where they can be found. Bring me all three and I will create a powerful enchantment for you!", "Zanza can create the ancient troll enchantments with the right components. This magic will help you in defeating Hakkar and his minions. I only ask that you bring me three items. I admit that one of these items is not entirely necessary but I wish to purge the world of the high elf magic." },
	["时间管理者"] = { "Beware, mortal, beyond this hall lies dangers unheard of in your world. Tread carefully...", "It is good to see you again, $N. Would you like me to take you to the master's lair?" },
	["明蒂·丁克斯"] = { "How may I help you?" },
	["星林长者"] = { "Last I knew, Elder Starsong was in the Sunken Temple of the Swamp of Sorrows.", "The Stars of this time are bent on new paths, beacons of hope and strength for the coming ages.", "Winterhoof? I hear he's living it up in Booty Bay." },
	["星歌长者"] = { "Elder Bellowrage watches over the Dark Portal from a ridge in the Blasted Lands.", "Elder Skychaser looks out over Westfall from atop Sentinel Hill.", "Elder Stormbrow is most likely at the village of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest.", "The Stars of this time are bent on new paths, beacons of hope and strength for the coming ages.", "Winterhoof? I hear he's living it up in Booty Bay.", "You'll find Elder Starglade outside the gates to Zul'Gurub in Stranglethorn Vale." },
	["星界商人图鲁曼"] = { "If you have come all the way out here, then it must be that you dare to venture near Manaforge Ara. Care to buy or sell before you head over?" },
	["星界商人拉斯莱"] = { "The World's End Tavern has nothing to offer those of my kind. However, I find that it attracts the type of clientele that are interested in what I have for sale. I specialize in exotic engineering goods acquired from far and wide. From time to time I might even have a rare thing or two for purchase. What might I interest you in?" },
	["星界商人玛里德"] = { "There are only 3 kinds of people in this world: competitors, customers, and employees. Competitors are to be crushed ruthlessly, customers indulged, and employees strictly supervised. Independent contractors are a myth.They want to be paid better than employees, but treated like customers. Never trust one who calls himself by that title." },
	["星界商人玛里德的影像"] = { "There are only 3 kinds of people in this world: competitors, customers, and employees. Competitors are to be crushed ruthlessly, customers indulged, and employees strictly supervised. Independent contractors are a myth.They want to be paid better than employees, but treated like customers. Never trust one who calls himself by that title." },
	["星界财团招募员"] = { "You look like a reasonable $r. Perhaps we could be of mutual assistance." },
	["星眼长者"] = { "Elder Dreamseer resides in Gadgetzan in Tanaris Desert.", "Elder Morningdew has taken to watching the commotion at the Mirage Raceway in Thousand Needles.", "Elder Ragetotem spends her days at the Valley of the Watchers in Tanaris Desert.", "In days long past, we lived for the hunt. We hunted for glory, for honor... Is it so different now?", "Zul'Farrak in Tanaris Desert is Elder Wildmane's home." },
	["星纹长者"] = { "Elder Bladeswift wanders the paths of Darnassus atop Teldrassil.", "Elder Nightwind passes the days at the shrine in Jaedenar in Felwood.", "The Stars of this time are bent on new paths, beacons of hope and strength for the coming ages.", "The village of Astranaar in Ashenvale is Elder Riversong's current home." },
	["春节预告者"] = { "Greetings, $N. We've travelled from Moonglade to spread the spirit of the Lunar Festival far and wide. Won't you join us in our celebration?" },
	["晕乎乎的迪娜"] = { "When you run with Razak's Roughriders, you learn a thing or two about following orders. The first thing is that you fight until you die. The second thing is, see the first thing." },
	["晨行者长者"] = { "Elder Rumblerock passes the years in a cave atop Dreadmaul Rock in the Burning Steppes.", "In days long past, we lived for the hunt. We hunted for glory, for honor... Is it so different now?" },
	["晨露长者"] = { "Elder High Mountain is at Camp Taurajo in the Barrens.", "Elder Mistwalker enjoys watching the struggles at the Maul in Feralas.", "Elder Moonwarden is observing the Crossroads in the Barrens.", "Elder Windtotem is keeping company with the goblins of Ratchet on the coast of the Barrens.", "Go to the Freewind Post in Thousand Needles and you will find Elder Skyseer.", "The Stars of this time are bent on new paths, beacons of hope and strength for the coming ages.", "You'll find Elder Grimtotem at the Lariss Pavilion in Feralas." },
	["普尔鲁"] = { "Memories of this temple shroud my mind like a thick haze, yet I cannot assemble them into a coherent story. This place meant something to me once. Until I can restore that memory, I will feel as though a part of me is missing. Perhaps the draenei can help me recover what I've lost." },
	["普希林"] = { "I hold the key to lands of free! Chase me and you'll see!" },
	["普拉特·马克格鲁比"] = { "Greetings $c -- if you're looking for leather goods and leatherworking supplies, you've come to the right semi-retired Paladin." },
	["普瑟尔·波利安"] = { "This isn't quite what I signed up for, but hey... at least it's warm here." },
	["普罗尼图斯"] = { "It is good to see you alive and well, $N!", "Thank you again for replenishing our healing crystals. I hear that you're helping out all over the place. Keep up the good work!" },
	["普莱瑟斯"] = { "*GRRRR* *RUFF* *RUFF*" },
	["普里克·斯韦尼"] = { "Welcome, friend, to the barbershop! Come for a cut? A coloring? Something else, perhaps? We can groom facial hair, perform piercings, ink night elf tattoos, and even reshape draenei horns and tendrils! Have a seat and we'll get right to work. You're only a few coins away from a new, more attractive you...", "Welcome, friend, to the barbershop! Come for a cut? A coloring? Something else, perhaps? We can groom facial hair, perform piercings, reshape tusks and horns, and even modify undead features! Have a seat and we'll get right to work. You're only a few coins away from a new, more attractive you..." },
	["普雷蒙"] = { "Oy, mon! This not be what it looks like. Well, maybe... It be complicated." },
	["晶歌森林护火者"] = { "Welcome, $c. Have you come to honor this flame? Remember: Our festival fires burn in every land with an Alliance settlement. Make time to honor each of them, if you can. The Horde, too, burns fires of their own. You would do well to desecrate such unworthy efforts when you see them." },
	["晶歌森林护焰者"] = { "Welcome, $c. Have you come to honor this flame? Remember: Our festival fires burn in every land with a Horde settlement. Make time to honor each of them, if you can. The Alliance, too, burns fires of their own. You would do well to desecrate such unworthy efforts when you see them." },
	["智者阿曼恩"] = { "Come closer, friend. Do not let my eyes startle you. I might have lost my sight many years ago but I never needed it to see the things that really matter." },
	["暗夜精灵平民"] = { "Dark times make for strange friendships. It may be worth visiting old Lordaeron to watch the Forsaken burn their little man of wicker.", "During Hallow's End we celebrate the day that the Banshee Queen herself delivered us from the clutches of the Lich King and the Scourge. Be sure to attend the Wickerman Festival that is held each evening outside Undercity.", "I do not understand the significance of the Forsaken burning a great wicker effigy each night, but our own rituals must seem just as strange to them.", "I don't know why the Forsaken burn a wicker man every night of Hallow's End instead of a real one, but it's their holiday.", "I understand this holiday is a creation not of our allies, but the Horde. Why we follow suit, I do not know.", "No other holiday matches the feasting and drinking of Brewfest!", "The Forsaken are right to celebrate their freedom. What else is more important?", "To celebrate the birth of yet another deadly enemy is an odd thing, to say the least. Still, we will join our allies in their festivities.", "We're celebrating the who breaking free of the what? Bah, who cares?! More candy!", "When Hallow's End is over we'll smash all these pumpkins. That'll be the greatest day I've ever known!", "Why does everyone keep saying the LAST thing we gnomes need is more sugar?!" },
	["暗夜精灵幽灵司仪"] = { "It's good to visit with friends and family again, celebrating and sharing stories of old." },
	["暗影主宰格里弗"] = { "Who do you think you are that you can walk in here and address me? I'm the leader of the Shadow Council in this village. Get out of my sight! If I see you again, I'll be the last person that you ever see. Understand? Perhaps you'd like to be buried in the labyrinth of Auchindoun, or sacrificed to Murmur?" },
	["暗影牧师范蒂丝"] = { "The time has come, my $g brother : sister; in arms, to take back the night from the Scourge!", "The time has come, my brother in arms, to take back the night from the Scourge!", "The time has come, my sister in arms, to take back the night from the Scourge!", "We are dominating the Scourge - the effects of the altered plague will affect them for at least another full day! We need to stay on top of it though, so be sure to sabotage a cauldron when you can.", "With the cauldrons breeched, we are now able to introduce the counter agent into the environment. This should give the scourge a taste of their own medicine, as it were! Check with Apothecary Dithers on information regarding the reagents needed to use in the cauldrons. I will be handling all information reports on how we are doing overall in turning the plague against the Scourge!" },
	["暗影牧师萨维斯"] = { "No other race on Azeroth has suffered as much as our people, $c. To laugh in the face of death has become second nature for all of us." },
	["暗影猎手德恩加"] = { "Welcome to Zabra'jin, $c. I am Shadow Hunter Denjai, overseer of this outpost and commander of the Darkspear forces in Zangarmarsh." },
	["暗月艺人"] = { "Don't forget to buy refreshments and souvenirs!", "Sure are a lot of litter bugs around here.", "The Darkmoon Faire is the greatest event on all of Azeroth!" },
	["暗灵长者"] = { "Elder Darkcore can be found in the Undercity.", "Elder Graveborn spends time near Brill in Tirisfal Glades.", "Elder Ironband lives in Blackchar Cave in Searing Gorge.", "Elder Moonstrike can be found in the Scholomance in the Western Plaguelands.", "Elder Wheathoof is enjoying the vistas above Mulgore at Thunder Bluff.", "Elder Windtotem is keeping company with the goblins of Ratchet on the coast of the Barrens.", "In days long past, we lived for the hunt. We hunted for glory, for honor... Is it so different now?", "Last I heard, Elder Runetotem was traveling to Razor Hill in Durotar.", "Now is the time when the year is new and the moon shines bright. It is our time... when the ancients awake." },
	["暗血监工"] = { "<The Murkblood overseer grunts.>", "I gladly make such a sacrifice if it means the downfall of the Dragonmaw.", "Overseer? You are no more an overseer than I am the king of Stormwind. Yes... You are the one they speak of.", "The Dragonmaw are corrupt. They are strip-mining this island of all natural resources and using those resources to supply Illidan's armies out of the Black Temple. They take much for themselves, however, and sell whatever they have hidden away to the highest bidder.", "The Netherwing. They speak to us. They offered us peace and protection. Something the broken have never truly felt. We accepted their offer and assisted Toranaku in rousing the creatures of this mine - at great personal cost to us. Many of my brothers gave their lives for this offensive. We were attempting to make the mine uninhabitable, forcing the Dragonmaw to relocate and ultimately move off of this island.", "They sent you to kill me, eh? So predictable... Creatures ruled by terror are all the same. But you... You are not one of them..." },
	["暗角长者"] = { "In days long past, we lived for the hunt. We hunted for glory, for honor... Is it so different now?" },
	["暮光演说者维克托尔"] = { "Welcome, $c. Have you come to honor this flame? Remember: Our festival fires burn in every land with a Horde settlement. Make time to honor each of them, if you can. The Alliance, too, burns fires of their own. You would do well to desecrate such unworthy efforts when you see them." },
	["暮色森林护火者"] = { "Welcome, $c. Have you come to honor this flame? Remember: Our festival fires burn in every land with an Alliance settlement. Make time to honor each of them, if you can. The Horde, too, burns fires of their own. You would do well to desecrate such unworthy efforts when you see them." },
	["暴怒图腾长者"] = { "Elder Dreamseer resides in Gadgetzan in Tanaris Desert.", "For reasons I cannot understand, Elder Thunderhorn has gone to the Slithering Scar in Un'Goro Crater.", "Go to the Freewind Post in Thousand Needles and you will find Elder Skyseer.", "In days long past, we lived for the hunt. We hunted for glory, for honor... Is it so different now?", "Zul'Farrak in Tanaris Desert is Elder Wildmane's home." },
	["暴风城冠军"] = { "Are you sure you are ready to fight a champion?", "Are you sure you are ready to fight me?", "It would be unwise to assume that fighting a champion would be a simple task. Are you sure you are ready?", "You've already bested one of our riders today, so I cannot accept your challenge." },
	["暴风城勇士"] = { "Are you sure you are ready to fight a valiant?", "Are you sure you are ready to fight me?", "It would be unwise to assume that fighting a valiant would be a simple task. Are you sure you are ready?", "You've already bested one of our riders today, so I cannot accept your challenge." },
	["暴风城卫兵"] = { "A Hunter is it? Well, then you will want to speak with Thorfin Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District. Oh, and you be sure to tell him that if I step in his pet's business one more time, he's going to be training other hunters from behind bars in the Stockade!", "A bank? Well, the closest bank around here is The Stormwind Counting House. It's just up the road in Stormwind not far from the gates.", "A rogue? Hmmm... well, I've heard that Keryn Sylvius hangs around those shady types. You might want to talk to her and see what you can learn.", "A tailor is it? Well, if you hang out here long enough you'll eventually hear word of mouth about Georgio Bolero. He's been setting the trends for some months now. If you wish to learn from him, you can find him over in the Mage Quarter in the outer rim.", "A warlock? Well, if I was a warlock, I would probably be in the darkest place around here... which would be the Lion's Pride Inn basement. That's where you should look first.", "Adele Fielder has made a name for herself as a leatherworker around Elwynn. You can find her working out of her home up by Crystal Lake.", "Ah, The Gilded Rose... with its soft down beds and warm baths... just thinking about that Inn makes me want to... ::yawn:: Lucky you if you're heading over there... you will find it in the west side of the Trade District. ...nice soft pillows, warm blankets. ::yawn::", "Ah, you're looking for Lucan Cordell. He runs a shop on the outside of the Magic Quarter on your way to the Stockade.", "Ahhh, Stormwind Visitor's Center is what you are looking for then. It's the first building on the left as you walk through the front gates from the Valley of Heroes.", "Ahhh, you are looking for Dungar Longdrink. He has some of the fastest gryphons this side of Khaz Modan! You can find him up on the ramparts in the Trade District.", "All of a sudden you're a 'Defender of the Alliance' are you?! Well, I suppose you'll be wanting to head to the Champions' Hall now. It's over in Old Town.", "All that official business is handled up in Stormwind these days. You could stop by the Stormwind Visitor's Center if you want to start a guild.", "Another entrepreneur, eh? Well, the Auction House can be found in the Trade District. Not far from the bank.", "Argus is the resident blacksmith of Goldshire. I'm sure he could teach you the Blacksmith's profession.", "Bah, rogues have done nothing but make our job here in Stormwind harder. I wish I could drag both Osborne and Mathias both out of Old Town and right to the Stockade.", "Brother Wilhelm often trains with Lyria Du Lac out in back of the smithy in Goldshire. You could probably learn a thing or two about being a paladin from him.", "Check around Old Town at the Barracks or the Pig and Whistle Tavern. If you go to the tavern, be sure to sample some of the fine brews. Puts the dwarven ales to shame, I tell ya.", "Duncan's Textiles employs one of the finest tailors in Stormwind, Georgio Bolero. Look for the shop over in the Mage Quarter.", "Eldrin is the only one in Elwynn Forest that I would call a tailor. You can find him at the Eastvale Lumber Camp if you're interested in learning the profession.", "Erma does all the caring for animals around here. She's right outside the Lion's Pride Inn if you need to speak with her.", "Few around here are as skilled with a blade as Lyria Du Lac. Check for her out behind the smithy and see if she's in the mood to teach you something new.", "Gelman Stonehand would be the one to talk to. I think he has a house over in the Dwarven District but I can't remember exactly. I would check over there.", "Gonna make a guild, are ya? Good luck to ya then! Talk to Aldwin Laughlin in the Stormwind Vistor's Center. It's in the Trade District right as you come in from the Valley of Heroes.", "Good ol' Erma, she's been taking care of the local animals for years now. I'm sure she'd be happy to take care of any you'd like to put up. She can be found right outside of the Lion's Pride Inn.", "Gryphons, eh? Never really cared for the beasts but to each their own. You can find Dungar Longdrink on the rampart in the Trade District.", "Helene Peltskinner has had years of experience skinning animals for Adele Fielder to make leather items. You can find Helene in her house by Crystal Lake.", "Hey, that reminds me, I need to have my rocket boots repaired. Word to the wise my friend, rocket boots and gryphons don't mix. Oh, but you need directions... just head on over to the Dwarven District, you'll find Lilliam Sparkspindle towards the back.", "Hmmm... only enchanters I know of around here work out of Stormwind. Why don't you ask one of the guards up in Stormwind?", "I believe Aldwin Laughlin is still the resident Guild Master of Stormwind. Look for his residence on your left as you pass the inner gate of Stormwind.", "I bet Josetta would be more than happy to teach you some new spells. She is probably up in her room at the Lion's Pride Inn.", "I don't know much about magic, but there's a mage named Zaldimar who is staying at the Lion's Pride Inn that could probably assist you.", "I don't know what's possessed you to look for a shaman... but I have seen someone who matches the profile. There's a woman who calls herself a Farseer on the shore in the Valley of Heroes.", "I had a bad encounter with some of the Defias around here recently, but Michelle Belle fixed me up pretty well. Check with her in the Lion's Pride Inn and see if she'll teach you.", "I know of a few people around here that practice a profession or two. What profession do you have in mind?", "I think you'll have better luck looking in Stormwind. Ask a guard up there and they'll point you in the right direction.", "I usually leave that sort of thing to the gnomes. If you want to take up the profession, I'm sure you could find some gnomes hanging out in Stormwind that would train you.", "I would suggest looking in the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "I'd wager Keryn Sylvius knows the type you're looking for. The company Keryn keeps is less than honorable. She usually hangs out in the Lion's Pride Inn.", "I've heard that there's a dwarf in Stormwind who has achieved some fame for his hunting skill. Maybe you should go see if he could help you.", "If you are looking to become a great cook, venture over to the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town and talk to Stephen Ryback. That man knows how to cook up a rack of ribs like no other. Man... now you got me hungry for some of his famous ribs. Don't count on him teaching you that recipe though!", "If you are looking to become a mighty paladin, there is no better teacher then Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker. He can be found in the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "If you need to house your pet while you're training another, then you should talk to Jenova Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District.", "If you need training in alchemy, there is only one place in Stormwind you need to go... Alchemy Needs. You can find it in the Mage Quarter along the outer rim of shops.", "It is located in the Trade District citizen. It is nearly straight on from the entrance of Stormwind.", "Jelenik's Barber Shop is in the northern section of the Trade District.", "Jelinik's Barber Shop is in the northern section of the Trade District.", "Jenova Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District is the one you're looking for. She tends to hunters' pets while they seek training from her father.", "Josetta has been a blessing to this town with her aid of the local guards. If you seek her for training in the ways of a priest, you can find her in the Lion's Pride Inn.", "Laurena is the High Priestess of Stormwind. You can find her in the Catheral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "Leave it to the dwarves to send a mining specialist from Ironforge to tell us how to mine. How hard is it to take a pick and chip away at some rock? Well, since he's here, he's probably the one you should see anyhow. His name is Gelman and he resides over in the Dwarven District.", "Lee Brown spends the whole day fishing up by Crystal Lake. He's probably got some stories to tell and some tips he could teach you.", "Lee's caught some pretty odd things up at Crystal Lake. He told me a story about this weird mask he fished up some months ago. If you ask me, I think he just had one too many at the Lion's Pride that night.", "Look no further than the Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire. With a wide selection of ales and soft down beds you, couldn't ask for a better place to rest.", "Lookin' to take a gryphon ride, eh? Dungar keeps his birds up on the rampart in the Trade District. Just remember to hold on tight!", "Looking for some training, eh? I could train you better then anyone in Stormwind but the guard prohibits it. I guess you will have to settle for one of those has beens hanging out around the Barracks or at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town.", "Lucan Cordell has a small shop on the canal by the Stockade. I am sure he will be able to teach you the art of enchanting.", "Lyria's the one you should talk to if you need some training. She can usually be found out behind the smithy waiting for some armor or weapon to be finished.", "Master Woo Ping has mastered nearly every weapon known to man. He is especially deadly with his sword techniques. He spends a good deal of time over in the Weller's Arsenal waiting on new shipments of weapons to arrive if you need some training.", "Michelle Belle's bedside manner is remarkable! While she might not be able to teach you that, she surely could teach you some proper First Aid. She currently resides in the Lion's Pride Inn.", "Ms. Pomeroy gathers herbs for an Alchemist who lives up in the hills between Northshire and Stormwind. Check for her at his cottage and see if she'll show you the profession.", "No better place to learn First Aid than under the watchful eye of Shaina Fuller at the Cathedral of Light. To get there, just look for the yellow rooftops, or the towering spire of the Cathedral itself which you can see from almost anywhere in the city.", "Nope, don't think there are any Enchanters here in Elwynn Forest. There's a guy named Lucan who runs a shop up in Stormwind though. You could check with him and see if he will train you.", "Nothing like spending a day down at Crystal Lake fishing. Arnold Leland is the man that taught me. You can usually find him out on the dock in the Canal District just fishing the day away. Oh, and don't believe any of the stories he tells you about monsters in the canals either.", "Oh, looking for some arcane enlightenment are you? No place better then then Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter.", "Oh, you must mean the Stormwind Counting House. It's not far from the gates after you enter Stormwind.", "Oh... one of those types. Well, Maximillian is the only one around here that knows about the dark arts. You can probably find him in the dark of the Lion's Pride Inn basement.", "Old Town is where you should go if you want to find rogues. It's in the northeast corner of Stormwind.", "Over by Crystal Lake there lives a lady named Adele Fielder. She makes patches for the local guards with the extra leather she gets from the local skinner, Helene. She would probably be the one to see if you're interested in learning the profession.", "Seek out Catarina Stanford in the canals southwest of The Stockade.", "Sounds like you want to talk to Maginor Dumas! You can usually find him in the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter. Course, you never know when or where those magi will portal off to.", "Stormwind Counting House is located by the front gates in the Trade District of Stormwind. And when you get tired of counting your money, be sure to stop by the Gilded Rose for a drink.", "Stormwind Counting House is located by the front gates in the trade district of Stormwind. And when you get tired of counting your money, be sure to stop by the Gilded Rose for a drink.", "Stormwind Harbor is the fastest way to get to Auberdine or Valiance Keep. You can find it between the Cathedral District and the Park.", "Stormwind's resident engineer trainer is an ingenious gnome by the name of Lilliam Sparkspindle. He can be found in the back of the Dwarven District.", "That bum Leland... all he does is sit out on the dock outside the Trade District and fish all day. I sure hope he's good at it for all the time he spends fishing. If you want to learn, why don't you go talk to him?", "That hermit Mallory is known to concoct some potions for the local townsfolk on occasion. He has a cottage in the hills between Stormwind and Northshire.", "The Bank of Stormwind is located in the Trade District just northwest of the city gates. Here, let me show you on your map.", "The Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square is home to the priests of Stormwind. There you will find High Priestess Laurena.", "The Cathedral of Light is the center of all the healing practices of Stormwind. There you can find Shaina Fuller to help you learn this craft.", "The Lion's Pride Inn in Goldshire is as good as any inn you will find around these parts. Drop in and let Innkeeper Farley make you feel at home.", "The Park is where you want to go if you are looking for druid trainers. Theridan and Maldryn can usually be found by the moonwell in the center of the district.", "The gryphon master oversees the gryphon flights from within Stormwind. If you're looking to take a ride, then that's where you should be headed.", "The magi congregate in the Wizard's Sanctum in the Mage Quarter. Quite a tower they have there. Makes our barracks look like peasant hovels.", "There are many establishments where you can get a drink in Stormwind, but only one will let you spend the night. Head over to the Gilded Rose in the Trade District. I've heard the cost of a room is reasonable and the sheets are clean.", "There are quite a few trainers available in Elwynn. Which one are you looking for?", "There is an alchemist that lives up in the hills between Northshire and Stormwind that might be of some help. Why don't you go pay him a visit?", "There is bound to be a gnome in Stormwind that can teach you the profession. I'm sure one of the Stormwind Guards could point you in the right direction.", "There's a great cook who works at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town. I've watched him use a knife when he cooks and just between you and me, I don't think he's always been a cook. Don't get me wrong... if you still want to learn, he's the best we have.", "There's an excellent skinner that lives up in the house by Crystal Lake. She's bound to be able to show you how to get started in the skinner's profession.", "There's an herbalist that lives in the hills east of Stormwind with our alchemist. Quite the handy pairing don't you think?", "Therum Deepforge is the dwarf you want to talk to. One of the finest blacksmiths around if you ask me. You can find him in the heart of the Dwarven District.", "Thorfin Stoneshield came to us all the way from Ironforge to bring us his expertise in hunting. If you don't mind breathing the smoke filled air of the Dwarven District then you'll find him at his house in the northeast area of the district.", "Tomas may not be the best cook around, but he has a few dishes that hit the spot. He's currently working in the Lion's Pride Inn if you'd like to learn the profession.", "Trying to reach Auberdine or Valiance Keep? You can find Stormwind Harbor if you head through the Canals, between the Cathedral District and the Park.", "Tucked away in the Mage Quarter, there is a little shop called Alchemy Needs. You're bound to see all sort of strange shops on your way through the Mage Quarter, but if you stick to the outer rim you'll be sure to find it.", "Want to learn leatherworking, eh? Simon Tanner would be able to teach you. He can be found in Old Town at the Protective Hide.", "Warlocks, eh. Well, you didn't hear it from me, but I've heard rumors that those types gather at a bar called the Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter.", "Warriors can usually be found either at the Pig and Whistle Tavern or the Barracks in Old Town. Tell ya though, the tavern is probably a better place to look.", "Well there's a gryphon master up in Stormwind if you need to fly somewhere. You should be able to see the gryphons landing on your right as you walk through the Valley of Heroes.", "Well, well, moving up in the world are we? You're looking for the Champions' Hall, and you'll find it on the southeast end of Old Town. Good luck!", "Well, you can find Theridan or Maldryn by the moonwell in the Park. Just head to the western area of Stormwind, north of the Mage District, but west of the Cathedral Square.", "What are you looking for?", "What do you need directions to?", "What? I don't know of any warlock trainers in Stormwind. Although... There have been some sightings of demonic activity over by The Slaughtered Lamb in the Mage Quarter. I suppose you could check there.", "Which class trainer are you looking for?", "Which profession trainer are you looking for?", "Why don't you try looking in the Lion's Pride Inn? The cook there might be able to teach you a few good recipes.", "Woo Ping's stamina is simply astounding. Watching him practice his weapon techniques for hours on end, I felt sorry for the practice dummy afterward. I can't think of anyone better suited to train you in armed combat.", "You are gonna want to head over to Old Town and drop by the Protective Hide if you are lookin' to learn skinning.", "You best head up to Stormwind in the Dwarven District if you want to learn to mine. Surely one of the dwarves there can teach you the profession.", "You can find Aldwin Laughlin at the Stormwind Visitor's Center in the Trade District.", "You can find Tannysa standing outside Alchemy Needs in the Mage Quarter.", "You can find the gryphon master on the northeast rampart overlooking the Valley of Heroes.", "You can usually find Brother Wilhelm in back of the smithy trading stories with Lyria. He's always up for teaching fellow paladins new skills.", "You don't have the stomach for the gryphon ride, huh. Well lucky for you, we have an alternative where you can keep your feet on the ground... more or less. It's the gnomish mover of people, the Deeprun Tram. Conveniently located in the back of the Dwarven District.", "You mean you can't smell the smoke of the Dwarven forges from here? Well, you will be looking for Therum Deepforge if you want to learn blacksmithing. He's over in the Dwarven District which is just north of the Cathedral Square.", "You must be looking for Smith Argus. He's usually overseeing the forge in Goldshire if you need some training.", "You want to learn to be a tailor? Hmmm... I believe there's a tailor over in the Eastvale Logging Camp that may be able to get you started.", "You want to talk to Osborne then. No finer teacher of the stealth arts than him in Stormwind. Look for him over in Old Town.", "You want what?! I've heard something about one of those odd draenei creatures in the Valley of Heroes. Maybe she knows; I don't.", "You'll be after Benik Boltshear, then. He's located in the heart of the Dwarven District by the blacksmiths.", "You'll find the battlemasters in the war room of Stormwind Keep.", "You're into leather, eh? Sounds like you should talk to Simon Tanner over in Old Town. He runs a shop there called the Protective Hide.", "You've heard about the Tram have you? What a ride that thing is! You'll find it in the Dwarven District towards the back. Oh, and be sure to keep your arms and legs inside the tram while the tram is in motion.", "Zaldimar could probably teach you some new spells. He has recently taken a liking to staying at the Lion's Pride Inn, you might want to check one of the rooms and see if he's in." },
	["暴风城巡逻兵"] = { "A Hunter is it? Well, then you will want to speak with Thorfin Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District. Oh, and you be sure to tell him that if I step in his pet's business one more time, he's going to be training other hunters from behind bars in the Stockade!", "A tailor is it? Well, if you hang out here long enough you'll eventually hear word of mouth about Georgio Bolero. He's been setting the trends for some months now. If you wish to learn from him, you can find him over in the Mage Quarter in the outer rim.", "Ah, The Gilded Rose... with its soft down beds and warm baths... just thinking about that Inn makes me want to... ::yawn:: Lucky you if you're heading over there... you will find it in the west side of the Trade District. ...nice soft pillows, warm blankets. ::yawn::", "Ah, you're looking for Lucan Cordell. He runs a shop on the outside of the Magic Quarter on your way to the Stockade.", "Ahhh, Stormwind Visitor's Center is what you are looking for then. It's the first building on the left as you walk through the front gates from the Valley of Heroes.", "Ahhh, you are looking for Dungar Longdrink. He has some of the fastest gryphons this side of Khaz Modan! You can find him up on the ramparts in the Trade District.", "All of a sudden you're a 'Defender of the Alliance' are you?! Well, I suppose you'll be wanting to head to the Champions' Hall now. It's over in Old Town.", "Another entrepreneur, eh? Well, the Auction House can be found in the Trade District. Not far from the bank.", "Bah, rogues have done nothing but make our job here in Stormwind harder. I wish I could drag both Osborne and Mathias both out of Old Town and right to the Stockade.", "Check around Old Town at the Barracks or the Pig and Whistle Tavern. If you go to the tavern, be sure to sample some of the fine brews. Puts the dwarven ales to shame, I tell ya.", "Duncan's Textiles employs one of the finest tailors in Stormwind, Georgio Bolero. Look for the shop over in the Mage Quarter.", "Gelman Stonehand would be the one to talk to. I think he has a house over in the Dwarven District but I can't remember exactly. I would check over there.", "Gonna make a guild, are ya? Good luck to ya then! Talk to Aldwin Laughlin in the Stormwind Vistor's Center. It's in the Trade District right as you come in from the Valley of Heroes.", "Gryphons, eh? Never really cared for the beasts but to each their own. You can find Dungar Longdrink on the rampart in the Trade District.", "Hey, that reminds me, I need to have my rocket boots repaired. Word to the wise my friend, rocket boots and gryphons don't mix. Oh, but you need directions... just head on over to the Dwarven District, you'll find Lilliam Sparkspindle towards the back.", "I don't know what's possessed you to look for a shaman... but I have seen someone who matches the profile. There's a woman who calls herself a Farseer on the shore in the Valley of Heroes.", "I would suggest looking in the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "If you are looking to become a great cook, venture over to the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town and talk to Stephen Ryback. That man knows how to cook up a rack of ribs like no other. Man... now you got me hungry for some of his famous ribs. Don't count on him teaching you that recipe though!", "If you are looking to become a mighty paladin, there is no better teacher then Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker. He can be found in the Cathedral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "If you need to house your pet while you're training another, then you should talk to Jenova Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District.", "If you need training in alchemy, there is only one place in Stormwind you need to go... Alchemy Needs. You can find it in the Mage Quarter along the outer rim of shops.", "It is located in the Trade District citizen. It is nearly straight on from the entrance of Stormwind.", "Jelenik's Barber Shop is in the northern section of the Trade District.", "Jelinik's Barber Shop is in the northern section of the Trade District.", "Jenova Stoneshield over in the Dwarven District is the one you're looking for. She tends to hunters' pets while they seek training from her father.", "Laurena is the High Priestess of Stormwind. You can find her in the Catheral of Light in Cathedral Square.", "Leave it to the dwarves to send a mining specialist from Ironforge to tell us how to mine. How hard is it to take a pick and chip away at some rock? Well, since he's here, he's probably the one you should see anyhow. His name is Gelman and he resides over in the Dwarven District.", "Lookin' to take a gryphon ride, eh? Dungar keeps his birds up on the rampart in the Trade District. Just remember to hold on tight!", "Looking for some training, eh? I could train you better then anyone in Stormwind but the guard prohibits it. I guess you will have to settle for one of those has beens hanging out around the Barracks or at the Pig and Whistle Tavern in Old Town.", "Lucan Cordell has a small shop on the canal by the Stockade. I am sure he will be able to teach you the art of enchanting.", "Master Woo Ping has mastered nearly every weapon known to man. He is especially deadly with his sword techniques. He spends a good deal of time over in the Weller's Arsenal waiting on new shipments of weapons to arrive if you need some training.", "No better place to learn First Aid than under the watchful eye of Shaina Fuller at the Cathedral of Light. To get there, just look for the yellow rooftops, or the towering spire of the Cathedral itself which you can see from almost anywhere in the city.", "Nothing like spending a day down at Crystal Lake fishing. Arnold Leland is the man that taught me. You can usually find him out on the dock in the Canal District just fishing the day away. Oh, and don't believe any of the stories he tells you about monsters in the canals either.", "Oh, looking for some arcane enlightenment are you? No place better then then Wizard's Sanctum 